Camellia rendezvous server configuration
----------------------------------------

The package does not start hbbs until /etc/default/camellia-server exists and
is non-empty. This is intentional: managed device registration requires an
API origin and a shared verification secret, neither of which can have a safe
package default.

Start from the packaged example:

  install -m 0640 -o root -g camellia-server \
    /usr/share/doc/rustdesk-server-hbbs/examples/camellia-server.env.example \
    /etc/default/camellia-server
  install -d -m 0750 -o root -g camellia-server /etc/camellia-server
  openssl rand -hex 32 | install -m 0640 -o root -g camellia-server \
    /dev/stdin /etc/camellia-server/device-verification-token

Replace the .invalid API and relay values, configure the same secret in the
Camellia API server, then run:

  systemctl enable --now rustdesk-hbbs.service rustdesk-hbbr.service

The key pair and SQLite database are shared in /var/lib/rustdesk-server and
are deliberately retained when a package is removed.
